{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "20442",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 1.25,
      "end_seconds": 5.51,
      "duration_seconds": 4.26,
      "text": "hi, is it okay to come in now?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 7.41,
      "end_seconds": 11.75,
      "duration_seconds": 4.34,
      "text": "no problem at all, come in what's troubling you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 13.56,
      "end_seconds": 19.93,
      "duration_seconds": 6.37,
      "text": "Hello doctor. I hope it's alright if I stay in for this."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 21.72,
      "end_seconds": 26.22,
      "duration_seconds": 4.5,
      "text": "Of course, please stay. It's helpful to to have you here."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 27.55,
      "end_seconds": 32.89,
      "duration_seconds": 5.34,
      "text": "doctor, um, it's breathlessness on exertion. That's what we're worried about"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 34.55,
      "end_seconds": 36.44,
      "duration_seconds": 1.89,
      "text": "When did this begin?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 40.09,
      "end_seconds": 51.04,
      "duration_seconds": 10.95,
      "text": "Honestly I can't say exactly when it started. It might have been last month or the month before, I really can't pin it down."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 52.27,
      "end_seconds": 57.13,
      "duration_seconds": 4.86,
      "text": "Okay, give me more detail on it, whatever comes to mind."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 58.33,
      "end_seconds": 61.15,
      "duration_seconds": 2.82,
      "text": "it's every other day. Mostly mild"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 62.86,
      "end_seconds": 68.25,
      "duration_seconds": 5.39,
      "text": "have you had a tight feeling in your chest when you walk uphill?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 69.43,
      "end_seconds": 70.94,
      "duration_seconds": 1.51,
      "text": "Yeah, that too."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 71.93,
      "end_seconds": 73.88,
      "duration_seconds": 1.95,
      "text": "How frequently does it come?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 75.86,
      "end_seconds": 85.29,
      "duration_seconds": 9.43,
      "text": "it's once or twice a day. I was feeling tired at one point but that's gone now"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 85.86,
      "end_seconds": 89.86,
      "duration_seconds": 4.0,
      "text": "right and what about pain at rest fainting or cough?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 91.11,
      "end_seconds": 93.43,
      "duration_seconds": 2.32,
      "text": "No I'd have said so."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 94.64,
      "end_seconds": 96.69,
      "duration_seconds": 2.05,
      "text": "and palpitations any of that?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 98.6,
      "end_seconds": 100.07,
      "duration_seconds": 1.47,
      "text": "nope, no palpitations"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 100.64,
      "end_seconds": 102.86,
      "duration_seconds": 2.22,
      "text": "is your mobility otherwise okay?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 104.16,
      "end_seconds": 105.72,
      "duration_seconds": 1.56,
      "text": "no, nothing there"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 119.29,
      "end_seconds": 123.65,
      "duration_seconds": 4.36,
      "text": "Tell me about your routine work habits that sort of thing."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 124.68,
      "end_seconds": 142.41,
      "duration_seconds": 17.73,
      "text": "I smoke roughly a pack every two days. Nothing, I'm teetotal. I grab fast food at lunch most days. I do a yoga class on Thursdays. My partner and our baby"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 143.29,
      "end_seconds": 145.94,
      "duration_seconds": 2.65,
      "text": "What's on your current medicine list?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 149.93,
      "end_seconds": 154.55,
      "duration_seconds": 4.62,
      "text": "she takes glibenclamide, 5 milligrams, before breakfast for my sugar"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 155.59,
      "end_seconds": 160.01,
      "duration_seconds": 4.42,
      "text": "I was on gliclazide before. I stopped taking it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 170.67,
      "end_seconds": 175.11,
      "duration_seconds": 4.44,
      "text": "what conditions have you been treated for in the past?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 176.65,
      "end_seconds": 179.2,
      "duration_seconds": 2.55,
      "text": "Yes, diabetes. Yes, high cholesterol."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 180.97,
      "end_seconds": 188.17,
      "duration_seconds": 7.2,
      "text": "right, so diabetes and high cholesterol are already on your record we'll keep that in mind today"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 190.78,
      "end_seconds": 194.26,
      "duration_seconds": 3.48,
      "text": "could you come over to the couch please?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 196.16,
      "end_seconds": 199.05,
      "duration_seconds": 2.89,
      "text": "take a a deep breath for me"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 214.11,
      "end_seconds": 217.42,
      "duration_seconds": 3.31,
      "text": "there is no swelling in your ankles"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 234.76,
      "end_seconds": 235.71,
      "duration_seconds": 0.95,
      "text": "Of course."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 236.53,
      "end_seconds": 239.25,
      "duration_seconds": 2.72,
      "text": "I'll listen to to your chest now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 253.84,
      "end_seconds": 259.22,
      "duration_seconds": 5.38,
      "text": "Heart sounds are normal, no murmur, and the chest is clear"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 265.17,
      "end_seconds": 273.27,
      "duration_seconds": 8.1,
      "text": "Okay, that's enough for me. So where does that leave us? This is probably exertional angina until proven otherwise."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 273.82,
      "end_seconds": 277.02,
      "duration_seconds": 3.2,
      "text": "do you think it's something serious?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 278.71,
      "end_seconds": 295.02,
      "duration_seconds": 16.31,
      "text": "I understand the worry at the moment I'd say it's exertional angina until proven otherwise, and we'll watch how it goes if the tightness comes, stop, sit down and use the spray under your tongue"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 296.24,
      "end_seconds": 300.22,
      "duration_seconds": 3.98,
      "text": "oh, should I have blood tests as well?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 300.91,
      "end_seconds": 321.96,
      "duration_seconds": 21.05,
      "text": "not right now, it it wouldn't change what we do today. If the chest pain lasts more than ten minutes or comes at rest, or you feel really unwell, please come to the emergency department. I'd like to see you again after the test results are back"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 322.66,
      "end_seconds": 325.04,
      "duration_seconds": 2.38,
      "text": "I can manage that that"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 327.04,
      "end_seconds": 331.9,
      "duration_seconds": 4.86,
      "text": "is there anything you'd like me to go over again?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 332.79,
      "end_seconds": 336.25,
      "duration_seconds": 3.46,
      "text": "Right, I'll do that. Thank you, doctor."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 336.89,
      "end_seconds": 338.72,
      "duration_seconds": 1.83,
      "text": "All the the best."
    }
  ]
}